  "_comment": "A shot list built around four effects rather than around a grade: an impact zoom out off a still, a shutter-shake into the first section, a film-roll into the second, and out-of-bounds onto the last shot. Two things in it are worth copying. The still opens letterboxed because the source photograph is 1.49:1 and a 9:16 crop would throw away two thirds of it. And each section is assembled from the clean stretches inside its span rather than played straight through: the source is an edited video whose own transitions fade to black, and a reel that plays those looks broken. scan_source.py finds them; `guard` refuses a range that straddles one.",
